android.extraProguardRules:
# Glance composes widgets through WorkManager; R8 strips OverwritingInputMerger's constructor without these keeps (verified on the 3T: the widget stays on its loading layout forever and logcat shows WM-InputMerger NoSuchMethodException)
-keep class androidx.work.** { *; }
-keep class androidx.glance.** { *; }
-dontwarn androidx.work.**
-dontwarn androidx.glance.**
# Expo 58 serves haptics and application through Modules v2: the host builds module classes from their no-arg constructors by reflection, the kolibri runtime reads its JNI bridge fields (NativeObject.nativePointer) from C++ alone, and the JSI dispatch reaches each module's @JS functions and argument types without a Java call graph for R8 to follow. io.github.expo ships no consumer rules for any of it, so R8 strips all of it (verified on the 3T: haptics never reach the vibrator; constructors alone crash at launch with NoSuchFieldError nativePointer; without the module packages the dispatch dies silently with VibrationType stripped)
-keep class io.github.expo.kolibri.** { *; }
-keep class io.github.expo.modules.v2.** { *; }
-keep class expo.modules.haptics.** { *; }
-keep class expo.modules.application.** { *; }
-keep class expo.modules.ExpoModulesV2ModuleList { *; }
